==[ MagazineCode Documentation ]==============================================

This is the technical documentation for MagazineCode for use with GunCode
based weapons and AmmoCode base rounds.

MagazineCode inherits NewThingCode, so functions like set_value(),
set_weight(), and the like can be found in new_thing.c

Any questions, bug reports, spelling corrections, or enhancement requests
should be addressed to Deathdealer.

=====[ Set Functions ]========================================================

void set_capacity( int cap )

     Used to set the number of rounds the magazine can hold.
     Default: 7


void set_ammo_type( string type )

     Used to set the ammunition type of the magazine.  Any ammo that is
     meant to be loaded into the magazine must have the same <type>.
     Default: ".22 caliber"


void set_mag_type( string type )

     Used to set the magazine type.  Any gun the magazine is meant to be
     used with must have the same <type>.
     Default: ".22 automatic"

void set_jam_chance( int jam )

     Used to set the extra jam chance when rounds are being fed into a gun
     from the magazine.  High capacity clips or oddly shaped magazines will
     tend to have a higher chance of jamming.
     Default: 1


void set_op_delay( int delay )

     Used to set the combat delay for loading a round into the magazine.
     Large bulky magazines, or clips with odd feeding mechanisms should have
     a higher operational delay to reflect the additional difficulty in using
     them.
     Default: 2


void set_slot_delay( int delay )

     Used to set the additional comabt delay when the magazine is loaded into
     a gun.  Simple clips will tend to have smaller slotting delays than
     awkward and cumbersome belts of ammunition, for instance.
     Default: 1


void set_queue( int queue )

     Used to set if the magazine holds rounds as a stack or a queue.  A normal
     clip for gun is a stack (you push rounds on to it), a belt of ammo for
     a large machine gun is a queue (you add more rounds to the end of it).
     Default: 0 (stack)


=====[ Query Functions ]======================================================

int query_capacity()

     Returns the number of rounds the magazine can hold.


string query_ammo_type()

     Returns the type of rounds the magazine can hold.


string query_mag_type()

     Returns the magazine type.


int query_jam_chance()

     Returns the extra chance of jamming when feeding rounds into a gun.


int query_op_delay()

     Returns the combat delay for loading rounds into the magazine.


int query_slot_delay()

     Returns the extra combat delay for loading the magazine into a gun.


int query_queue()

     Returns if the magazine is queue based (1), or stack based (0).

object *query_ammo()

     Returns the ammo objects currently loaded in the magazine.


object query_shot()

     Returns the next shot that will be loaded into a gun.


int query_shots()

     Returns the number of shots currently left in the magazine.


int query_value()

     Returns the value of the magazine plus the value of any ammunition
     currently contained in it.


int query_weight()

     Returns the weight of the magazine, plus the weight of any ammunition
     currently contained in it.


=====[ Utility Functions ]====================================================

varargs void fill_with( string filename, int num )

     Call this function in extra_create() when you want to fill the magazine
     with a specific ammunition object (otherwise the magazine will start out
     empty).  <num> is an optional argument if you want to specify the number
     of rounds to add, otherwise <num> will default to the magazines capacity.
     
     Example:
     
     extra_create() {
       ...
       fill_with( "/obj/weapon/gun/ammo/223_tracer", 3 );
       fill_with( "/obj/weapon/gun/ammo/223" );
       ... }
       
     This would put three tracer rounds in the magazine (to be fired last
     unless the queue flag is set), and then fill the magazine to capacity
     with normal .223 rounds.


=====[ Optional Functions ]===================================================

int extra_jam( object gun )

     Overload this function if you want something special to happen to the
     magazine in the event of a gun jam.

